# glossary.txt.example — hotword glossary for the speech-to-text recognizer.
#
# Copy this file, fill in expected names/terms for your own meetings, and
# point SCRIBE_GLOSSARY at your copy (see scribe.conf.example):
#
#   cp glossary.txt.example glossary.txt
#   export SCRIBE_GLOSSARY="/path/to/glossary.txt"
#
# Format:
#   - One hotword or phrase per line.
#   - Blank lines are ignored.
#   - Lines starting with "#" are comments and are ignored.
#   - Order doesn't matter.
#
# What to put here: attendee names, project/product names, acronyms, or any
# term the recognizer is likely to mishear or spell inconsistently — biasing
# it toward these terms up front tends to work better than fixing typos in
# the transcript after the fact.
#
# Example (uncomment/edit, or just add your own lines below):
# Alice
# Bob
# Acme
# Zephyr
